# Labelled definitions and rules with a condition, written on one line

Formatting must be idempotent: the condition starts a new line, so the label
is followed by a line break too.

```catala
declaration scope A:
  context c content duration
  output d content date
  output f condition

scope A:
  label r definition d equals |2024-01-31|
  exception r
  definition d
  under condition c > 0 day
  consequence equals
    |2024-01-01|
  label base
  definition d
  under condition c > 10 day
  consequence equals
    |2024-01-02|
  label q
  rule f
  under condition c > 0 day
  consequence fulfilled
  exception q
  rule f
  under condition c > 1 day
  consequence not fulfilled
  exception base
  definition d
  under condition c > 2 day
  consequence equals
    |2024-01-03|
```
